{"type":"text","timestamp":1793604125640,"sessionID":"ses_e64deede2ffe3MZ2QGYcb33oEx","part":{"id":"prt_19b22ba2e001P1Yx0yuWMQtwtM_text-0","sessionID":"ses_e64deede2ffe3MZ2QGYcb33oEx","messageID":"msg_19b22ba2e001P1Yx0yuWMQtwtM","type":"text","text":"Done — `result.json` is written.\n\n**What I did**\n- Loaded `./METRICS.md` rules: steps install → tutorial_complete → first_match → purchase; a step counts only if its event occurs at or after the player's previous step's time (no time limit); test accounts and events from unknown players excluded; conversion = step players / previous step players; biggest drop = lowest conversion.\n\n**Assumptions I made (brief was silent on these)**\n1. **Install step** = users who have a valid `install` event. 123 non-test users (593→470 pc, 273→192 steamdeck) have later events but no install event, so they don't enter the funnel — consistent with \"a step counts only at or after the previous step.\"\n2. **\"First valid occurrence\"**: for each step I took the earliest event that is at/after the previous step's valid time (not just the earliest event overall). This matters: 26 users have out-of-order event sequences, and 14 purchases only count under this rule (e.g. a purchase before a re-logged tutorial still counts).\n3. Events from unknown players can't attach to any user, so they're excluded by construction; `is_test=1` users excluded.\n\n**Findings (per platform)**\n- **PC**: 470 → 389 → 326 → 269. Biggest drop: **purchase** (82.5% conversion, 57 players lost).\n- **Steam Deck**: 192 → 128 → 87 → 61. Biggest drop: **tutorial_complete** (66.7% conversion, 64 players lost).\n\n**Why I trust it**: the numbers were computed with a single pass enforcing the METRICS.md ordering rule per player; I cross-checked edge cases (no-install users, out-of-order sequences, unknown-player events) directly in SQL before finalizing. Interesting nuance: the naive \"first event, no ordering check\" method would have flagged PC's purchase step differently (0.78 vs 0.83) and hidden Steam Deck's real problem at tutorial completion — the ordering rule genuinely changes the answer.","time":{"start":1793604106801,"end":1793604125640}}}
